## Required Imports

### Core Imports
```java
import java.io.Serializable;
import com.fasterxml.jackson.annotation.JsonFilter;

import core.connect.api.input.ConnectInputRepresentation;
import core.connect.resources.ConnectInputProperty;
import core.connect.resources.ConnectInputRep;
import core.connect.resources.ConnectWrapperDefinition;
import core.connect.resources.IConnectContext;
```

### Optional Imports (Based on Requirements)
```java
import com.fasterxml.jackson.annotation.JsonProperty;
import javax.validation.Valid;
import javax.validation.constraints.*;
import java.math.BigDecimal;
import java.util.List;
```

## Class Structure

### Class Declaration Template
```java
@ConnectInputRep(
    description = "Connect API representation of [purpose]",
    topLevelInputRepresentationXmlTagName = "[xmlTag]",
    wrapper = @ConnectWrapperDefinition(className = "[ClassName]"))
@JsonFilter(IConnectContext.JSON_FILTER)
public class [ClassName]InputRepresentation 
    extends ConnectInputRepresentation 
    implements Serializable {
    // Class contents
}
```

### JavaDoc Template
```java
/**
 * Connect API representation of [purpose]
 *
 * @author [username]
 * @since [version]
 */
```

## Annotations

### Class Level
- `@ConnectInputRep`: Defines API representation metadata
- `@JsonFilter`: Applies JSON filtering
- `@Valid`: For nested object validation

### Field Level
- `@ConnectInputProperty`: Documents field properties and version
- `@JsonProperty`: Customizes JSON field names
- Validation annotations as needed:
  - `@NotNull`
  - `@Size`
  - `@Pattern`
  - `@Email`
  - `@Min`/`@Max`
  - `@DecimalMin`/`@DecimalMax`

## Field Patterns

### Standard Field Structure
```java
private [Type] fieldName;
private boolean isSetFieldName;

public [Type] getFieldName() {
    return fieldName;
}

@ConnectInputProperty(
    description = "Description of the field",
    minVersion = [version])
public void setFieldName([Type] fieldName) {
    this.fieldName = fieldName;
    this.isSetFieldName = true;
}

///CLOVER:OFF
public boolean _isSetFieldName() {
    return isSetFieldName;
}
///CLOVER:ON
```

### Nested Class Structure
```java
public static class NestedClass implements Serializable {
    private [Type] field;
    private boolean isSetField;
    
    // Getters, setters, and isSet methods
}
```

## Best Practices

### 1. Field Naming
- Use camelCase for Java fields
- Use `@JsonProperty` for snake_case JSON mapping
- Prefix boolean tracking fields with "isSet"

### 2. Type Selection
- Use primitive wrapper classes (Integer, Boolean) instead of primitives
- Use BigDecimal for monetary values
- Use String for dates (format: YYYY-MM-DD)
- Use List<T> for collections

### 3. Version Control
- Always specify minVersion in @ConnectInputProperty
- Increment version numbers appropriately for new fields

### 4. Documentation
- Include clear descriptions in @ConnectInputProperty
- Document all public methods and classes
- Include usage examples in class-level JavaDoc

### 5. Validation
- Add appropriate validation annotations
- Include meaningful validation messages
- Validate nested objects with @Valid

### 6. Code Coverage
- Mark isSet methods with ///CLOVER:OFF and ///CLOVER:ON
- Ensure all fields have corresponding isSet methods

### 7. Error Handling
- Include appropriate validation annotations
- Use meaningful error messages
- Consider adding custom validators when needed

